Z||000000||85ZainoGT||11-03-2001||04:17 PM||||Anyone got any ideas how I can make my 87gt(that I am buying soon) faster off the line? and.. just faster  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> not to expensive things though, just little things that add up...<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1985 White/Silver GT <BR>2.8L 4 Speed LOADED :)<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sigpic2529_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Borgio||11-03-2001||04:42 PM||||My dad always says that nothing simple and easy works. They design them the best they can right from the factory. They could have made them with more power, but if there was something simple and fuel efficient they would've done it. The best thing you can do to a fiero for cheap is port the exhaust manifold, that adds a couple horsepower, but you have to get the exhaust off to do that. The exhaust is really restricted at the top of the manifold. It was really just a design flaw, I think. But anyone doing a swap or that has their engine out, I would recomend that.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cutlass207TDC||11-03-2001||06:49 PM||||You can get an air-intake or even a K&N filter which will let your car breath a little better.  Exhaust can help you out too.  Finally a computer chip can do a great job.  This shouldn't cost too much. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||SKIDMARK||11-03-2001||10:30 PM||||Port the exhaust manifolds. You can do this for free or maybe the cost of gaskets at home if your handy with tools. Leave the intake alone, except maybe a new filter. Pontiac engineers did a pretty good job with the intake and the computer. Besides, that stuff cost $ that you probably already spent buying the car. Wait till you can afford major improvements like a cam or maybe a 3.4 or 3800 transplant. Research everything you can about turbos, superchargers, etc. before you make a decision about performance improvements. Good luck with your new purchase!<P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||3
Z||000004||85ZainoGT||11-03-2001||10:38 PM||||thanks for the info so far guys!! What do you think about poly dog bones and power pulleys?  would that help out a little bit?  and a torque converter?  the thing is, I want it to be AT LEAST as fast as my 85gt 4 speed is from the line and from 45mph...<p>[This message has been edited by 85ZainoGT (edited 11-03-2001).]||||reg||1
